123 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (And all such voluntary actions come down to what we consider certain phantasms to be pleasurable and certain phantasms to be painful. All acts are preceded by desire. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
124 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 89 0 R
/E (It may not be proper to call them voluntary either. All voluntary actions are just simply the last desire you have after you cancel out competing desire. My act of reaching buy an orange from the market is preceded by a competing desire to just stay in the bed or watch a TV show. But I may want an orange so bad that I just override all other desires and settle on this one. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
125 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 89 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/A [224 0 R 0]
/K [4]
>>
endobj
126 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 90 0 R
/T (A Leviathan Called Desire: )
/E (A Leviathan Called Desire: )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
127 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (It is quite commonsensical to assume that I want my desires to be fulfilled. Thus, I may buy the orange and lay on my bed while watching the TV. But desires are rarely so confined. In a minute I want some water. The orange is not sweet enough so I crave some litchis. I will then find out ways to get all of them. The finding in order to getting is what Hobbes though that reason does. It finds the shortest path to achieve all my desires. )
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
128 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (But maybe, I am walking down the store to buy litchis and they are almost out of stock except the last packet. But another customer wants to buy it too. What do I do? I want it more than them so our desires are in competition. Do I bash their head?)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
129 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 90 0 R
/E (A state prevents that to happen.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
130 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 90 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/A [225 0 R 0]
/K [4]
>>
endobj
131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 91 0 R
/T (A Leviathan Called Desire: )
/E (A Leviathan Called Desire: )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (A state prevents people from eating each other alive over litchis and oranges. Maybe I win the fight but tomorrow my competitor may bring ten people to beat me up. I will live in constant anxiety and thus any pleasure I had from winning that packet of litchi is overturned by my fear of being beaten up. This state is what Hobbes called the state of nature. It is when humans have absolute liberty and basic equality that leaves them at this constant anxiety.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 91 0 R
/E (So, naturally because we gravitate to that which is more pleasurable, we decide that the state of nature is not feasible. And so, comes The Leviathan. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
134 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 91 0 R
/Pg 19 0 R
/A [226 0 R 0]
/K [3]
>>
endobj
135 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 92 0 R
/T (The State:)
/E (The State:)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
136 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 92 0 R
/E (The Leviathan is borne out of contract between consenting humans who realized that the state of nature is not worth it. Humans contract exclusively with one another to surrender their right of self-governance to The Leviathan. But, the Leviathan is not a party in the contract. It is not appointed. A participant in a contract is limited by the contract. If I decide to give my competitor an orange as a sorry, they are also limited by being a recipient of the orange. The State has absolute sovereignty. The state preserves the contract between me and my competitor. It is in its domain to decide whether an orange is sufficient or whether it is not right for my competitor to ask for apples as well. )
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
